{
  "about": "Each shape one Worker hands another over RPC that a strict parser reads, by its name: the Worker that builds it (from) and the one whose parser refuses any field it does not list (to); the fields it hands every time (required), every time but taken as if optional (always: the step between optional and required, either way), when it has them (optional), and the ones taken that are not handed (dropped: handed by a release before, or not yet). Each parser reads its fields here (contract/src/handed.ts) and nowhere else. The deploy kit deploys each Worker after the ones it binds (deploy/facts.ts WORKERS), so while the earlier of the two serves this tree's version, the later still serves its version before: where the parser deploys first, it must take everything the sender's version before hands; where the sender does, the parser's version before must take everything it hands. deploy/handed.ts holds this file, beside the door table, to that, against the base branch (deploy/guards/handed.test.ts) and against the versions the stage serves (the kit's plan). A field is dropped (or made always) first, and goes once the versions the stage serves no longer need it.",
